    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "This podcast is brought to you by the North Dakota Petroleum Foundation. From heating our homes and powering our vehicles to cell phones, clothing, and medical equipment, oil and natural gas makes everyday life better. North Dakota oil and natural gas, advancing the possibilities, learn more at ndpetroliumfoundation.org. Welcome to plain talk live. I'm your host Rob Port and joining me is Congressman Kelly Armstrong, who for a brief moment, not long ago was going to be a member of, you know, probably one of the most high profile congressional committee, I guess a commission is what we're calling it. Since the 9 11 Commission, I mean, it's a pretty important. What I felt was going to be a pretty important initiative. The Republican minority in the House of Representatives appointed members of that commission, speaker of the House, Nancy Pelosi decided she didn't like some members of that commission. And what ended up happening is Republicans pulled all of their appointees from the commission. Now that commission is proceeding, it does have some Republicans on it, but their Republicans appointed, not by the leader elected by the House Republican caucus, but by the leader of the Democratic caucus. here to talk with me about that, of course, is Congressman Kelly Armstrong and Kelly, you had a, you were, you were going to be on the commission and then you weren't, I have your statement that you, that you pub put out after this whole thing went down. This is your July 21 statement. I quote Jim Banks and Jim Jordan. Now these are the two members of the commission that, that, of course, Speaker Pelosi didn't want on there. Jim Banks and Jim Jordan have every right to serve in any committee leader McCarthy appoints them to. Whenever Speaker Pelosi uses the word unprecedented, it is code for her consolidation of absolute power. She is willing to do anything and everything, the main control over her conference for the next 18 months. In the process, she is going to permanently and negatively change the way this body functions forever. I think that last point, this whole thing was, I think going to be an exercise in ranked partisanship. from the get-go. Um, that being said, I'm not so sure that your last point isn't the most important one, which is that there's a long tradition of, you know, everybody in the House of Representatives is there because their constituents elected them. They're there by the will of the people. And then each caucus, the Democratic caucus, the Republican caucus, Alexa leader, right? This is how the whole thing's organized. Nancy Pelosi just threw she said a precedent whereby the majority party can decide which members can serve on a committee and it just doesn't matter what the minority party has to say about it at all that's that's a terrible thing a dangerous thing i think",
