    "turn_text": "their constituents and essentially half of the country unfairly. They're not a lot of minority rights that you have as members of Congress. And every member in the minority party represents a constituency of essentially the same size. And if you allow Speaker Pelosi to populate the committees, four Republicans on any of this, you are essentially silencing the voice of millions of people from one end of the country to the other. And listen, if these, you know this, I know this, when you make decisions like this, it never goes back to the way it was. And this is a very, and also as somebody who served and was a criminal defense attorney, your dad was in law enforcement. The hardest cases are when you have to make sure your rules, your procedures and your traditions work. because hard cases make bad law and we fundamentally change things. This is unprecedented. It is a power grab. A lot of people talk about this about the last election or the next election. I really don't believe that's the case. I believe when you, on Tuesday, Speaker Pelosi's majority went down to three votes. They are very rowdy and rambunctious caucus on their side. They have a lot of differing viewpoints. This is about maintaining control. One of the few things that every Democrat in DC can agree on is hating President Trump. And this allows them to do that in this way, but it also means 50% of this country is just not going to take anything that happens out of that committee seriously.",
