    "turn_text": "another thing, because you put this in a legal context, but let's put it in a larger sense, in a nation where we are obligated to work with one another. I'm fond of saying that one of the prices of living in a free society is that you're going to hear and see some things you don't like sometimes. You know, that's the First Amendment, right? It means the person you disagree with has to say, that's the democratic process as well too. Sometimes you're going to have to work with people. You don't like that much. Sometimes you're going to have to work with people that just fundamentally disagree with you, just can't even agree with you on the most basic things. And yet what what democracy charges us with is working with those people anyway. And what Nancy Pelosi said is to heck with that, we don't have to do that.",
