  {
    "episode_id": 47141,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47141.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Well, there was intelligence as early as December 14th as something was going on. There was an intelligence memo on January 3rd saying that some of this was going on. During the middle of the day, there was a truck parked outside with riot gear that they couldn't get into because it was locked. I'd have several questions. Why wasn't it handed out? But I think my questions for the officers would have been, did you know about any of these things? Because we know they existed and they were on the ground. They didn't know the protocol that they had for deploying the National Guard as Capitol Police leadership. You're going to have a lot of political shots thrown back and forth on this, and that's how this works, right? It's a political hearing, but there are real fundamental questions that go all the way back actually to our Judge Kavanaugh's confirmation, Rob. Rob, that line got broke at that time. The acting chief of police after January 6 was the acting or was the intelligence offered prior to January 6. There are real questions that need to be answered, and we need to have answers to them so we make sure it never happens again.",
