    "turn_text": "and I think one of the points of this and all of this is, you know, we, I did it. I did partisanship for, I mean, we did the Mueller investigation to impeachments. We had Michael Coleman and oversight and just, just because there's partisanship in there doesn't mean things don't come out. Doesn't things don't come up. I think we make a bigger mistake in this town when we try and pretend anything isn't partisan I think that's I think that's a political fish in we put out to try listen Nothing about these things looks resembles anything in a courtroom anywhere in the country civil criminal federal state local of that and to pretend that it does is just being this again being dishonest with the American people It can be partisan and it can still be fact finding, but to your original answer, I don't know. I would doubt very seriously that they're gonna pursue avenues that get objective in the middle, but we haven't seen, I don't even know when the next hearing's gonna be, but I like you will be paying attention. I will watch every bit of these that I can because I think regardless of everything else, it's important to know what's being said and how it's being portrayed and whether it's factual, whether it's got political to it, and I think it's important.",
