    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "it does frustrate me that a lot of times, you just said, you know, it doesn't resemble anything like a courtroom. Well, nor should it. It's not a courtroom. It's a partisan, it's Congress. Congress is not a courtroom. And then this is frustrated me because it seems like with the impeachment proceedings, with a lot of the things that we've been doing, that the Kavanaugh hearings, we've been trying to make it seem like these congressional hearings or these committee, that they're a courtroom, You know, and we talk about things like due process and all this stuff. And listen, these are important philosophical concepts, but they're trying to imbue these fundamentally political proceedings with the more objective proceedings, far more objective, institutionally objective proceedings of the criminal justice system. And that's such a canard. I don't like it at all. Do you feel like, I mean, what understanding that this commission's not done It may yet illuminate some things perhaps that we don't know or don't fully understand yet. That being said, what would you like to see happen going forward at the Capitol once this is all over and it's time maybe to make some policy?",
