    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47141.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "too often. The internet is not free. It's never been free. It's really not free right now. You supply your contract with the internet using it is you will have all kinds of data about you collected and monetized by somebody else. That is how the internet remains. That's how the internet remains able to be used without paying for it. But you are paying for it. I'm paying for it. We're paying for it right now. just by being able to host this. And we're going to have to start talking about that in a better way, because net neutrality, all of these different issues, tend to view the internet as a free service. And it really is not a free service.",
